        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Agra</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1504 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">An ancient city on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> is lost in the legends of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikandar-lodi">Sikandar Lodi</a> rebuilt Agra in 1504–1505, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> founded the modern city on the right bank in 1558.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> river in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, about 230 kilometres south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, in the Braj region.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> seat of government; the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>; the Agra Fort; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taj-mahal">Taj Mahal</a>; the tombs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> and Itmad-ud-daulah; Akbar's Din-i-Ilahi; the rebellion of 1857</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Agra is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a> with a population of 1,585,704 at the 2011 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">census</a>, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taj-mahal">Taj Mahal</a> and Agra Fort are <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-heritage-site">World Heritage Sites</a>.</span></div>
